 /// A neighbor cache backed by a map.
+///
+/// Discovery requests are rate-limited **per protocol address**: after a request for an
+/// address, the next request for that same address waits [`Cache::SILENT_TIME`], while
+/// requests for other addresses go out at once. At most `IFACE_NEIGHBOR_CACHE_COUNT`
+/// addresses can be silenced at a time; when all of them are, a lookup of any other missing
+/// address is rate-limited too, so the request rate never exceeds that many per
